l_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Verify canary release\n\n- [X] I verified that the issue exists in the latest Next.js canary release\n\n### Provide environment information\n\n```\r\nOperating System:\r\n  Platform: win32\r\n  Arch: x64\r\n  Version: Windows 10 Home\r\nBinaries:\r\n  Node: 18.14.1\r\n  npm: 9.2.0\r\n  Yarn: N/A\r\n  pnpm: N/A\r\nRelevant packages:\r\n  next: 13.2.2-canary.0\r\n  eslint-config-next: N/A\r\n  react: 18.2.0\r\n  react-dom: 18.2.0\r\n```\n\n### Which area(s) of Next.js are affected? (leave empty if unsure)\n\nApp directory (appDir: true), Routing (next/router, next/navigation, next/link)\n\n### Link to the code that reproduces this issue\n\nhttps://github.com/darthrommy/typedroute-catches-routegroups\n\n### To Reproduce\n\n1. Run `npm run dev`\r\n2. Wait for `.next/types/link.d.ts` to be generated\n\n### Describe the Bug\n\nRoute groups are hidden from the actual route hierarchy, but are included in the auto-generated `Route` type.\r\n\r\nIn my example, routes are defined like this:\r\n\r\n1. `/page.tsx` -> `/`\r\n1. `/foo/page.tsx` -> `/foo`\r\n1. `/(group)/bar/page.tsx` -> `/bar`\r\n\r\nBut I got type error when using `next/link`:\r\n\r\n```tsx\r\n// works fine\r\n<Link href=\"/foo\">To Foo</Link>\r\n\r\n// throws error\r\n<Link href=\"/bar\">To Bar</Link>\r\n\r\n// does not throw\r\n<Link href=\"/(group)/bar\">To Bar</Link>\r\n```\r\n\r\nYou can also confirm that the `/(group)/bar` type is generated by looking at `.next/types/link.d.ts`.\r\n\r\n```ts\r\ntype Route<T extends string = string> = \r\n  | `/${Suffix}`\r\n  | `/(group)/bar${Suffix}`\r\n  | `/foo${Suffix}`  | `/${Suffix}`\r\n  | `/(group)/bar${Suffix}`\r\n  | `/foo${Suffix}`\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Temporary Workaround\r\n```tsx\r\n<Link href={\"/bar\" as Route}></Link>\r\n```\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nI think route groups should be ignored by route type generations.\n\n### Which browser are you using? (if relevant)\n\n_No response_\n\n### How are you deploying your application? (if relevant)\n\n_No response_","closed_by":{"login":"kodiakhq[bot]","id":49736102,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk3MzYxMDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29196?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kodiakhq%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/kodiakhq","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kodiakhq%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kodiakhq%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kodiakhq%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kodiakhq%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kodiakhq%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kodiakhq%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kodiakhq%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kodiakhq%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kodiakhq%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/46401/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/46401/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}